Summary 
Highly Available Applications
•	Designed to resist failures or conditions that could make them unavailable.
•	Kubernetes/OpenShift ensures traffic only reaches healthy pods.
________________________________________
Health Probes
•	Readiness probes: Ensure a pod is ready before sending traffic.
•	Liveness probes: Detect and restart unhealthy pods.
•	Proper probes prevent requests from failing during startup or crashes.
________________________________________
Resource Requests and Limits
•	Requests: Minimum guaranteed CPU/memory for scheduling pods.
•	Limits: Maximum CPU/memory a pod can consume.
•	Helps balance cluster node resources and prevents resource exhaustion.
________________________________________
Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA)
•	Automatically scales the number of pod replicas.
•	Scaling decisions based on metrics such as CPU or memory utilization.
•	Parameters include:
o	minReplicas and maxReplicas
o	target utilization (e.g., 60% memory usage)
________________________________________
✅ Takeaway:
•	Combine probes + resource requests/limits + HPA to make applications reliable, responsive, and efficient under varying loads.


